  "rationale": "S4 sim-playability (2026-10-08): deliberate behaviour changes and three content edits. (1) laborObligation: the occupation demand restates the subsistence (food) and upkeep (vellum) bills at the land's own yield share before dividing by a laborer's all-kinds output; before, it asked for under half the laborers the food bill needs and the reference universe starved at a 47% shortfall from about world year 150 (origin/main 95738881, seed 20260813). Fed universes grow larger and their mages reach further. (2) Stagnation's quiet clock: a tick is quiet when no node entered and no paid god intervention landed; it ends a run after 480 quiet ticks only while worship is below the health floor and below the universe's own peak tier (decline), or after 1200 quiet ticks whatever worship reads (neglect, new constant stagnation-neglect-ticks). (3) rl-open-the-portal researchCost 18343 -> 9520, the tier-4 floor. (4) change-tradition favorCost 65536 -> 61440, the tier-4 cap. (5) readEdicts returns ascending handle order, the order action 7's resolver indexes. The provenance-only re-seal was not attempted on this 200-year gate: the 20-year agency gate's re-seal was refused on referencePeakPopulation (+8.0 SE) on this branch, and this gate measures the same population and knowledge series over ten times the horizon, where the food change compounds. This is the new behaviour, not a regression.",
